'''Jamal Murray''' (born February 23, 1997) is a Canadian professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Denver Nuggets]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played one season of [[college basketball]] for the [[Kentucky Wildcats men's basketball|Kentucky Wildcats]]. Murray was selected by the Nuggets as the seventh overall pick in the [[2016 NBA draft]] and was a key contributor to the team's first [[NBA championship]] run in [[2023 NBA Finals|2023]], becoming the ninth Canadian to win an NBA title.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pells |first=Eddie |date=June 12, 2023 |title=Canada's Jamal Murray an NBA champ as Nuggets top Heat for 1st title |url=https://www.cbc.ca/sports/basketball/nba/denver-nuggets-miami-heat-game-5-nba-finals-recap-1.6873506 |access-date=October 18, 2025 |work=CBC Sports}}</ref> In 2026, Murray was named an [[NBA All-Star]]. He is also a member of the [[Canada men's national basketball team|Canadian national team]].

